::Question 1::
If we enter the try: block, it implies that _____
{
~ The block will be omitted
~ All of the instructions from this block will be executed
= Some of the instructions from this block may not be executed
~ None of the instructions from this block will be executed
}

::Question 2::
Which statement is used to raise an exception in Python? 
{ 
~ except Exception()
~ throw Exception()
= raise Exception()
~ catch Exception()
}

::Question 3::
What is the correct syntax to catch an exception in Python?
{
= except Exception
~ catch Exception
~ try Exception
~ handle Exception 
}

::Question 4::
What is the purpose of an else block in a try-except-else statement?
{
= To execute code if an exception is not thrown  
~ To execute code if an exception is thrown  
~ To execute code regardless of whether an exception is thrown  
~ To execute code after the try and except blocks are executed
}
